Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-05-2000||10:07 PM||||  It's time too smog the GT and it wont pass. I have a crushed EGR tube and the vacuum lines to the Vacuum regulator are not connected to any thing(Regulator is missing). Bought a new tube $47.oo and a vacuum regulator $57.00, Solves that problem right? WRONG! The single hose off of the regulator goes....Where? My chiltons manual doesn't show a very good dipiction of the vacuum system. I need to know where that line is supposed to go. Can anyone help? Ilove tinkering with this car and you all have made it so much easier. I appriciate every bit of help I recieve from the forum; what a great place.<P>Thanx B-B ||||reg||11
Z||000001||ka4nkf||03-05-2000||10:27 PM||||That single line goes to the air cleaner. there should be a fitting on the canister or the snorkel tube. If you cant locate it dont worry about it . It is only a clean air line and your vac control has a filter in it anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||03-05-2000||11:54 PM||||  Not to question...But, are you sure? The air cleaner is on the opposite firewall. I just want to be sure. <P>  Thanx :0) B-B||||reg||5
Z||000003||ka4nkf||03-06-2000||12:11 AM||||Look at todays post by 86 fiero (where does that small black hose go) there is a picture of it. It does go to the air cleaner. It originaly went to the firewall and connected to a metal tube that wen to the air cleaner. like i said dont worry about it , it is not important||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||03-06-2000||06:39 AM||||After you get your EGR system fixed use some octane booster for your smog test, it's supposed to help a whole bunch.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||03-06-2000||10:22 AM||||Also turn on your rear window defogger or A/C switch. This is a cheat because the ECM thinks the vehicle is under load and adjusts your fuel and timing. This is why they always tell you to turn off all accessories. ||||reg||1
